  "review": {
    "note": "Re-audited all direct build, runtime, optional development and Node dependencies for the markerless-discovery correction. The dependency manifest and every registry candidate are unchanged from the reviewed 0.24.0 receipt. Third-party latest candidates satisfy declarations and support Python 3.14. The documented coordinated-core exception remains: registry h2hdb 0.36.1 is below the >=0.37.0,<0.38.0 requirement, and validation uses the locally built h2hdb 0.37.0 wheel without a committed sibling path. No new third-party release requires another release-note review. The compatible fix removes numeric-name inference: new markerless folders remain traversal nodes until a marker appears; existing published locators still receive fresh existence checks and retain published observations while incomplete. This avoids perpetual waiting on numeric collection directories. Full fast checks, 86 focused filesystem/marker/monitor/snapshot tests and seven real SQLite publication/restart/retry tests passed. No schema, observation codec, library format, dependency contract or compatibility shim changes. The exact-tree gate separately records bounded offline pytest, Lean, finite TLC and installed-wheel validation; live MariaDB results are separate manual evidence.",
    "status": "reviewed"
  },
  "schema": "h2h.dependency-audit.v1"
